Valkey 8.0 release notes
========================

Upgrade urgency levels:

| Level    | Meaning                                                             |
|----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| LOW      | No need to upgrade unless there are new features you want to use.   |
| MODERATE | Program an upgrade of the server, but it's not urgent.              |
| HIGH     | There is a critical bug that may affect a subset of users. Upgrade! |
| CRITICAL | There is a critical bug affecting MOST USERS. Upgrade ASAP.         |
| SECURITY | There are security fixes in the release.                            |

Valkey 8.0.13  -  Released Wed 18 November 2026
-----------------------------------------------

Upgrade urgency SECURITY: This release includes security fixes we recommend you apply as soon as possible.

### Security Fixes
* CVE-2026-130822: Fix a use-after-free crash in client eviction when maxmemory-clients is enabled by @nadav-levanoni (#5435)

### Bug Fixes
* Fix a crash during eviction sampling, and hangs, crashes, or duplicate set members in key comparison, when a key name or member reaches 2 GiB by @madolson (#5133)
* Correct command metadata to describe the `ZINCRBY` increment and `ZINTER`/`ZINTERSTORE`/`ZUNION`/`ZUNIONSTORE` weights as doubles instead of integers by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#5210)
* Propagate `PFADD` elements applied before a corrupted-HLL INVALIDOBJ error so replicas and the AOF stay consistent with the primary by @madolson (#5128)
* Fix a server panic when a Lua script returns or raises an error table whose metatable has an `__index` metamethod that raises an error by @madolson (#5118)
* Fix a server crash when a module never sets a postponed reply length; the leftover placeholder is now filled with an empty array by @madolson (#5159)
* Mark the `RESTORE` and `RESTORE-ASKING` `IDLETIME` and `FREQ` options as mutually exclusive in command metadata by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#5212)
* Fix `PFMERGE` with no source keys bypassing ACL key permissions and failing in `COMMAND GETKEYS`, and a crash in module commands whose keynum key spec starts past the last argument by @madolson (#5087)
* Fix `SCRIPT KILL` and `FUNCTION KILL` not stopping Lua scripts that loop inside nested coroutines, and script timeouts not being detected when work is spread across coroutines by @madolson (#5108)
* Fix a crash in a cluster replica whose primary was removed from the nodes table when another primary claims an unassigned slot by @madolson (#5184)
* Fix an out-of-bounds write in `PFADD` and `PFMERGE` on a corrupted sparse HyperLogLog ending in a truncated XZERO opcode by rejecting it as invalid by @madolson (#5124)
* Fix a server abort in `PFADD` and `PFMERGE` on short sparse HyperLogLogs when `hll-sparse-max-bytes` is set to 31 or less by @madolson (#5138)
* Fix a server crash in `SORT` and `SORT_RO` with `BY` or `GET` patterns when an element is 2 GiB or larger by @madolson (#5146)
* Fix `ValkeyModule_Calloc` and `ValkeyModule_TryCalloc` returning an undersized buffer when `nmemb * size` overflows; `Calloc` now panics and `TryCalloc` returns NULL by @madolson (#5155)
* Fix `ValkeyModule_CallReplyAttributeElement` always returning an error on RESP3 attribute replies by @madolson (#5157)
* Fix `EXEC` succeeding after a key that was already expired at `WATCH` time is overwritten, which can happen on replicas by @madolson (#5169)
* Fix a memory leak when `server.register_function` named arguments are repeated in a different letter case by @madolson (#5120)
* Generate a new shard_id when the replica executes CLUSTER RESET SOFT by @enjoy-binbin (#2283)
* Correct expiry command metadata to show that `XX` can be combined with `GT` or `LT`, rather than all four conditions being mutually exclusive by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#5213)
* Fix a memory leak when a script or module command is refused by ACL while the ACL log is disabled with `acllog-max-len 0` by @madolson (#5162)
* Fix `notify-keyspace-events` dropping the `n` (new key) flag from `CONFIG GET` and `CONFIG REWRITE` when `A` is also set by @pirate329 (#5199)
* Fix a cluster node failing to restart with an assertion after a gossip entry carrying the MYSELF flag adds a second myself node to nodes.conf by @madolson (#5134)
* Fix `ACL LOAD` not disconnecting default user clients subscribed to channels the reloaded rules no longer allow by @madolson (#5085)
* Fix a memory leak in `ValkeyModule_GetCommandKeysWithFlags` when introspecting commands with large key lists by @christopherlim98 (#5046)
* Bound the time spent per cycle evicting keys from the client tracking table, avoiding long stalls after lowering `tracking-table-max-keys` by @tanmayBeginsJourney (#4775)
* Correct `ZADD` and `LCS` metadata so `COMMAND DOCS` and valkey-cli hints no longer present `NX` with `GT`/`LT` or `LEN` with `IDX` as valid combinations by @rainsupreme (#5244)
* Correct `SENTINEL SIMULATE-FAILURE` metadata so `COMMAND DOCS` shows the required mode argument and its tokens by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#5208)
* Fix a Sentinel crash when a monitored replica's `INFO` reply contains no `master_host` by @smkher (#4929)
* Fix a TLS busy loop that consumed 100% CPU when a connection's read or write handler was removed while OpenSSL was waiting for the opposite event by @yairgott (#3510)
* Fix a crash caused by a NULL pointer dereference when all timer events in an event loop are pending deletion by @royenheart (#4351)
* Fix a node staying stuck in PFAIL when its PING is lost while the peer's own traffic keeps the cluster link alive by @enjoy-binbin (#4171)
* Fix `SORT` key extraction so a `STORE` destination named like an option can no longer bypass ACL checks and write to an unauthorized key by @madolson (#4665)
* Fix `GEOSEARCH` returning empty results for exact zero-distance matches on builds where floating-point contraction breaks the latitude distance calculation by @Baraa-Hasheesh (#4777)
* Fix a crash in active defrag when a database's keyspace is replaced mid-scan, for example by `FLUSHDB ASYNC`, `SWAPDB`, or a replica's flush before a full sync by @taham0 (#4968)
* Fix a crash when a replication role change command such as `REPLICAOF` or `CLUSTER REPLICATE` arrives over a replication link by @madolson (#5187)
* Fix `XADD` rejected for oversized elements leaving an empty stream on the primary that is never propagated to replicas or the AOF by @madolson (#5178)
* Fix unbounded memory growth in the client tracking table by reclaiming IDs of disconnected clients for keys that are never modified, and include the table in active defrag by @rayjinghaolei (#4190)
* Redact credentials of rejected `HELLO`, `AUTH` and `MIGRATE` commands so passwords no longer leak to MONITOR and the commandlog by @madolson (#5180)
* Ignore invalid ping extension values from cluster peers that would corrupt nodes.conf and prevent the node from restarting by @madolson (#5137)
* Bound the bytes the cluster bus reads per event so a peer with a constant read backlog cannot starve clients, cron and heartbeats by @madolson (#5161)
* Fail `CONFIG REWRITE` when the old config file reads short instead of writing uninitialized memory into the new config file by @madolson (#5158)
* Prevent a replica crash when the primary wrongly replies +CONTINUE to a full resync request; the replica now drops the link and retries by @madolson (#5126)
* Fix a crash on 64-bit builds when `LSET` merges list nodes whose combined size exceeds 4GB, reachable with lists loaded through `RESTORE` or a full sync by @madolson (#5163)
* Fix a use-after-free in streams when `XADD` creates a new node, which could leave a dangling pointer hit by later reads such as `XRANGE` by @Baraa-Hasheesh (#4711)
* Reject inbound cluster bus packets larger than 16MB, except Pub/Sub and module messages, so a peer cannot make a node buffer up to 4GB from a single header by @madolson (#5065)
* Fix `XINFO GROUPS` and `XINFO STREAM ... FULL` reporting too-high consumer group lag after `XTRIM` or a trimming `XADD` removes unread entries by @Sasidharan3094 (#4983)
* Fix AOF load failure after a crash leaves a torn annotation at the end of the file; it is now treated as a short read and can be truncated by `aof-load-truncated` or `valkey-check-aof --fix` by @sumitk163 (#5349)
* Correct the `SENTINEL GET-MASTER-ADDR-BY-NAME` reply schema to allow the null reply returned for an unknown primary name by @rainsupreme (#5246)
* Fix a use-after-free crash when client eviction under `maxmemory-clients` frees a client that is still executing a command which unblocked another client by @nadav-levanoni (#5435)
* Fix a crash after `REPLICAOF NO ONE` with TLS and a connection leak after `REPLICAOF` to a new primary when the old primary client is freed asynchronously due to pending I/O by @yaronsananes (#3719)

Valkey 8.0.12  -  Released Mon 26 October 2026
----------------------------------------------

Upgrade urgency SECURITY: This release includes security fixes we recommend you apply as soon as possible.

### Security Fixes
* GHSA-f4q9-j22m-xqq9: Fix a heap buffer overflow in cluster Pub/Sub message construction that could allow an authenticated client to potentially execute arbitrary code by publishing an oversized message by @roshkhatri (#5030)

### Bug Fixes
* Fix stream commands that mutate consumer-group or PEL state (`XGROUP`, `XSETID`, `XREADGROUP`, `XACK`, `XCLAIM`, `XAUTOCLAIM`) not triggering `WATCH` and client-side tracking invalidation by @Tarte12 (#3459)
* Fix a server abort on a RESTORE payload declaring a string length that overflows the allocation size; such payloads are now rejected as bad data by @enjoy-binbin (#4733)
* Reject module write commands while the server is paused for writes, preventing a crash from module timer callbacks during `CLIENT PAUSE WRITE` or `CLUSTER FAILOVER` by @smkher (#3645)
* Fix ZINTER/ZINTERSTORE returning input-order-dependent scores when a weighted term is 0*inf; a NaN weighted score now counts as 0, matching ZUNION by @leomurillo (#4997)
* Correct `ValkeyModule_FreeModuleUser`, `ValkeyModule_ACLAddLogEntry` and `ValkeyModule_ACLAddLogEntryByUserName` declarations to return int as implemented, fixing undefined behavior on targets with strict call signature checks by @rainsupreme (#4676)
* Fix valkey-benchmark spinning on would-block writes, which could starve reply processing and the `--duration` timer by @thweetkomputer (#4567)
* Fix a huge memory allocation when a command such as COMMAND GETKEYS EVAL declares a far larger key count than the arguments provided by @murphyjacob4 (#3598)
* Reject relative expire times in `SET`/`GETEX`, `RESTORE`, and `ValkeyModule_SetExpire` that overflow when added to the current time, preventing server aborts from negative expires by @madolson (#4880)
* Fix a server crash when loading an ACL file containing a selector with an unmatched parenthesis by @magic-peach (#4214)
* Sorted set range commands with a negative `LIMIT` offset now return an empty result instead of a spurious element on btree-encoded keys by @xiaocj (#4637)
* Redact error text in server logs when `hide-user-data-from-log` is enabled, so command arguments no longer leak into logs by @zackcam (#4815)
* Fix cluster config saving to avoid publishing truncated `nodes.conf` files, losing the startup lock after the first save, and failing every save on SMB filesystems such as Azure Files; the lock now lives on a separate `nodes.conf.lock` file by @KewangZhili (#4489)
* Fix `LSET` on 64-bit builds silently modifying the wrong element for out-of-range indexes instead of returning an index out of range error by @charsyam (#4823)

Valkey 8.0.11  -  Released Mon 31 August 2026
---------------------------------------------

Upgrade urgency SECURITY: This release includes security fixes we recommend you apply as soon as possible.

### Security Fixes
* GHSA-jcj7-v34w-v9vv: Fix a use-after-free in RDMA connection handling that could allow an authenticated client to crash the server using CLIENT KILL. Only affects servers built with USE_RDMA and configured with an RDMA listener (#4534)

### Bug Fixes
* Fix a double-free crash when a module timer callback stops its own timer with `ValkeyModule_StopTimer` by @quanyeyang (#4211)
* Fix AOF truncation after a partially persisted MULTI/EXEC block so writes made after recovery are not lost on a later restart by @chzhoo (#4342)
* Fix an ACL bypass where duplicate STORE/STOREDIST options in GEORADIUS commands let users write keys outside their permitted patterns by @tjade273 (#3971)
* Fix a use-after-free crash when a cluster message for a module-registered type arrives after the module is unloaded by @enjoy-binbin (#4360)
* Fix out-of-bounds access on cluster module messages of type 255, which is now a valid message type by @enjoy-binbin (#4410)
* Fix silent data loss where ACL checks were wrongly applied to commands replayed from the AOF file by @lukepalmer (#3984)
* Fix a client memory accounting leak that inflated the `mem_clients_normal` INFO field on replicas by @enjoy-binbin (#4395)
* Always deep-validate listpack payloads on RDB load and RESTORE, preventing deferred assertion crashes; `sanitize-dump-payload` is deprecated and now a no-op by @jjuleslasarte (#3721)
* Fix module `VM_Yield` timing so repeated yields honor `busy-reply-threshold` instead of the server hz interval by @PingXie (#2131)
* Fix a stack overflow crash when a large TLS write is retried after an OpenSSL write error by @murphyjacob4 (#4307)
* Fix a crash caused by forged cluster bus PUBLISH or MODULE packets carrying oversized payload length fields by @tjade273 (#3972)
* Reject crafted stream payloads in RDB load and RESTORE whose length or field-count metadata is inconsistent, preventing later server panics by @madolson (#3922)
* Fix a cluster link disconnect loop after network failures that caused pub/sub messages between nodes to be lost by @dvkashapov (#2817)
* Fix a use-after-free crash when a client blocked on a key is freed while other clients blocked on the same key are being served by @quanyeyang (#4212)
* Reject crafted stream payloads that misstate live and deleted record counts, preventing data loss on XDEL by @roshkhatri (#4381)
* Fix incorrect `CLUSTER SLOT-STATS ORDERBY` ordering when slot statistics differ by more than 2^31 by @jzy1688 (#4459)

Valkey 8.0.10  -  Released Tue 21 July 2026
-------------------------------------------

Upgrade urgency SECURITY: This release includes security fixes we recommend you apply as soon as possible.

### Security Fixes
* CVE-2026-56684: Fix a use-after-free in TLS connection handling that could allow an authenticated client to crash the server using CLIENT KILL (#4234)
* CVE-2026-63639: Reject corrupt stream RDB files containing a shared NACK across consumers. Reported by @z0v3r1n and @lifip. (#4073)

### Bug Fixes
* Strictly validate CRLF line endings when parsing the RESP protocol, rejecting malformed requests as protocol errors by @enjoy-binbin (#2872)
* Fix memory leak in `ZDIFF`/`ZDIFFSTORE` when the result set becomes empty before all input sets are processed by @sarthakaggarwal97 (#3342)
* Fix crash caused by a race between asynchronous client freeing and IO threads reading from the closing client by @deepakrn (#3458)
* Fix double free when loading corrupt stream RDB data containing duplicate consumer PEL entries by @enjoy-binbin (#3498)
* Fix stream corruption and crash when `XTRIM` marks the last entry of a listpack node as deleted by @smkher (#3591)
* Fix potential crash in TLS pending-data handling when the connection has no SSL object by @zuiderkwast (#3641)
* Fix use-after-free when `ACL LOAD` removes a user whose authenticated client's free is deferred by @ranshid (#3800)
* Fix use-after-free when a module unregisters the first-registered cluster message receiver for a message type by @eifrah-aws (#3846)
* Fix crash when loading functions after `FUNCTION FLUSH ASYNC` and make `FUNCTION FLUSH` actually release Lua VM memory by @enjoy-binbin (#1826)
* Fix file descriptor leak when a blocking connect times out, such as `MIGRATE` to an unreachable host by @madolson (#3541)
* Fix crash in module LRU/LFU API functions (GetLRU, SetLRU, GetLFU, SetLFU) when passed a NULL key by @yaronsananes (#3610)
* TLS synchronous I/O no longer leaves a blocking socket in non-blocking mode, preventing unexpected short reads by @xbasel (#1298)
* Fix crash when `CLUSTER SLOTS` is called without a real client connection, such as from a module timer callback by @bandalgomsu (#2915)
* Fix assertion crash in the IO thread job queue on ARM/aarch64 caused by memory store reordering by @jjuleslasarte (#3878)
* Reject zipmap `RESTORE` payloads with overflowing length fields that could cause out-of-bounds access on 32-bit builds by @madolson (#3920)
* Reject NAN scores in listpack and ziplist encoded sorted sets on RDB load, preventing a later crash on skiplist conversion by @madolson (#3921)
* Fix crash on 32-bit systems where time_t is 64-bit (e.g. Alpine with time64) when generating INFO output by @chenshi5012 (#3787)
* `COMMAND INFO` in RESP3 now returns an empty Array instead of a Set for the subcommands field of commands without subcommands by @rickrams (#3939)
* Manual failover votes are no longer restricted by two times the node timeout, preventing manual failover timeouts by @enjoy-binbin (#1305)
* Automatic failover votes are no longer restricted by two times the node timeout, matching the manual failover change by @enjoy-binbin (#1356)
* `SENTINEL SET` now rejects values containing control characters and config rewrite escapes them, preventing config injection by @eifrah-aws (#3847)
* Reject control characters and delimiters in cluster AUX fields and `cluster-announce-ip` to prevent nodes.conf injection by @eifrah-aws (#3848)
* Fix `lua-enable-insecure-api yes` not taking effect when set at startup via config file or command line by @enjoy-binbin (#3548)
* Log 'Connection reset by peer' instead of the misleading 'Success' when the connection to the primary closes during sync by @abmathur-ie (#3580)
* Redact key names and user data from additional server log messages when `hide-user-data-from-log` is enabled by @zackcam (#3872)
* Increase the maximum process title length from 255 to 1024 characters to avoid truncation with long paths by @pkhartsk (#3843)
* `valkey-cli --cluster del-node` can now remove unreachable or failed nodes instead of failing with 'No such node ID' by @yang-z-o (#3209)
* Fix `valkey-cli --cluster` assigning all uncovered slots to the same primary instead of distributing them randomly by @abmathur-ie (#3586)

